@startuml
title 13.5 In-App Notifications - sequence diagram
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

actor "Logged-in user" as U
participant "View" as V <<View>> #EADCFF
participant NotificationController as C <<Controller>> #D8F3DC
participant NotificationService as S <<Service>> #DCECFF
participant NotificationRepository as R <<Repository>> #FFF1C9
participant ChatService as CH <<Service>> #DCECFF
database MySQL

== A. Load the bell (on page load and when the logged-in user changes) ==
V -> C : GET /api/account/notifications
C -> S : mine(userId)
S -> R : findByUserIdOrderByCreatedDateDesc(userId)
R -> MySQL : SELECT Notifications of the user, newest first
MySQL --> R : rows
R --> S : List<Notification>
S --> C : List<NotificationResponse>
C --> V : 200 OK
V -> C : GET /api/account/notifications/unread-count (sent together with the list)
C -> S : unreadCount(userId)
S -> R : countByUserIdAndReadFalse(userId)
R -> MySQL : SELECT COUNT(*) WHERE is_read = false
MySQL --> R : count
R --> S : count
S --> C : count
C --> V : 200 OK {"count": n}
V --> U : red dot when n > 0; unread rows highlighted; "Không có thông báo nào." when empty
note over V
  Errors are only logged to the console, the bell keeps its previous state.
  No timer: new notifications appear after a page reload.
end note

== B. Open the bell: mark all as read ==
U -> V : click the bell
V -> V : toggle the dropdown
alt unread count is 0
  V -> V : no request
else unread count above 0
  V -> C : PUT /api/account/notifications/read-all
  C -> S : markAllAsRead(userId)
  S -> R : markAllAsRead(userId)
  R -> MySQL : UPDATE Notifications SET is_read = true WHERE user and is_read = false
  C --> V : 204 No Content
  V -> V : count = 0, all rows shown as read
end
note over V
  The click handler runs on every click, so closing the dropdown also calls it (no request when count is 0).
  If the request fails, the badge stays and the error is only logged.
  There is no request that marks one notification as read.
end note

== C. A notification is created (example: new chat message) ==
CH -> R : findFirstByUserIdAndLinkOrderByCreatedDateDesc(recipientId, link)
R -> MySQL : SELECT latest notification with the same link
MySQL --> R : row or none
R --> CH : Optional<Notification>
alt latest notification with this link is still unread
  CH -> CH : skip, no new bell item
else none, or already read
  CH -> S : notifyUser(recipient, "Tin nhắn mới", "<name> vừa gửi tin nhắn cho bạn.", link)
  S -> R : save(Notification: id, user, title, message, link)
  R -> MySQL : INSERT Notifications
end
note over CH
  Runs inside ChatService.send (@Transactional): the notification commits with the message.
  Order, payment, refund and occasion notifications call the same NotificationService methods
  (see the class note); they are not repeated here.
end note

@enduml
